---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Glossary of Indian Debt & Credit Terms"
  description="Definitive legal and financial glossary of Indian credit terminology: DPD, NPA, SARFAESI, OTS, haircut, eNACH, EBLR, and CIBIL reporting metrics."
  showSidebars={true}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <span class="meta-tag">Terminology</span>
    <h1 class="page-title">Indian Debt & Credit Glossary</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">
      Precise statutory and financial definitions of terms used across Reserve Bank of India lending directions, credit reporting manuals, and recovery enforcement statutes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose">
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem;">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Annual Percentage Rate (APR)
        </h2>
        <p>The annualised total cost of credit expressed as a percentage, encompassing not merely the nominal interest rate but all mandatory upfront processing fees, documentation charges, verification fees, and recurring administration costs over the tenure.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Compromise Settlement (One-Time Settlement - OTS)
        </h2>
        <p>An agreement between a lender and a distressed borrower wherein the lender accepts a negotiated lump-sum amount less than the total outstanding contractual debt to settle the account, writing off the remaining balance as a haircut.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Credit Information Company (CIC)
        </h2>
        <p>An institution licensed by the Reserve Bank of India under the Credit Information Companies (Regulation) Act, 2005 to aggregate, maintain, and generate credit reports and scores. India has four licensed CICs: TransUnion CIBIL, Experian, Equifax, and CRIF High Mark.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Days Past Due (DPD)
        </h2>
        <p>A credit bureau reporting metric that indicates the exact number of calendar days an installment, EMI, or credit card minimum payment has remained unpaid beyond its contractual due date. Typical categories include 000 (current), 030 (1–30 days overdue), 060, and 090+ (default/NPA).</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Debt Avalanche
        </h2>
        <p>A debt elimination methodology wherein all surplus discretionary monthly cash flow is directed toward paying off the loan account carrying the highest Annual Percentage Rate (APR), while paying contractual minimums on all other accounts. Mathematically guaranteed to minimize total cumulative rupee interest outflow.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Debt Snowball
        </h2>
        <p>A debt elimination strategy wherein all discretionary repayment funds are directed toward paying off the account with the lowest absolute principal balance first, regardless of interest rates, to secure rapid psychological momentum and reduce the total number of open debt obligations.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Debt Recovery Tribunal (DRT)
        </h2>
        <p>A specialized quasi-judicial tribunal established under the Recovery of Debts and Bankruptcy Act, 1993, possessing exclusive jurisdiction to adjudicate debt recovery claims exceeding ₹20 Lakhs initiated by banks and to hear borrower appeals against SARFAESI possession under Section 17.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          eNACH (Electronic National Automated Clearing House)
        </h2>
        <p>A web-based standing instruction payment system managed by the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI) allowing banks to automatically debit recurring loan EMIs from a customer's savings account. Dishonour of an eNACH mandate attracts criminal liability under Section 25 of the Payment and Settlement Systems Act, 2007.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          External Benchmark Lending Rate (EBLR)
        </h2>
        <p>The mandatory benchmark rate to which all retail floating-rate term loans (home loans, personal loans) sanctioned by commercial banks must be linked pursuant to RBI directives (typically the RBI Policy Repo Rate), ensuring transparent transmission of monetary policy adjustments.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Haircut
        </h2>
        <p>The percentage or rupee amount of a loan's outstanding contractual liability that a lending institution voluntarily agrees to waive or write off as an uncollectible loss during a compromise settlement (OTS).</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Key Fact Statement (KFS)
        </h2>
        <p>A standardized, mandatory summary document that all regulated lenders in India must provide to a borrower before loan agreement execution, detailing the net disbursement, gross principal, all-inclusive APR, EMI schedule, and grievance redressal officer contacts.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Minimum Amount Due (MAD)
        </h2>
        <p>The contractual floor amount that a credit cardholder must pay by the monthly due date to prevent the account from being classified as delinquent and to avoid late payment charges. Typically calculated as 5% of balance or (100% of finance charges + 18% GST + 1% principal).</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Non-Performing Asset (NPA)
        </h2>
        <p>A loan or advance facility where the payment of principal or interest has remained overdue for a continuous period of more than 90 calendar days under Reserve Bank of India prudential asset classification norms.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          SARFAESI Act, 2002
        </h2>
        <p>The Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest Act, 2002; empowers secured creditors (banks and HFCs) to take possession of and auction mortgaged security interests without approaching a civil court upon default.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-emerald); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0;">
          Wilful Defaulter
        </h2>
        <p>A formal penal classification defined under RBI Master Directions for borrowers who deliberately default on debt obligations despite possessing financial capacity, or who divert/siphon loan funds for unapproved speculative purposes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
